  "description": "The Real Me is the tenth studio album by American rapper Future. Released on July 10, 2026, through Freebandz and Epic, it is Future's first solo studio album in four years, following I Never Liked You (2022), and his first full-length solo project since Mixtape Pluto (2024). The album was produced by Allen Ritter, ATL Jacob, DJ Spinz, Dre Moon, FnZ, Pharrell Williams, RushDee, Sean Momberger, Southside, TM88, and Wheezy, among others. Similarly to his last project, Mixtape Pluto, it contains no features.",
